'''wake-time''' (wāk′tīm), ''n.'' Time during which one is awake. ''Mrs. Browning'', Aurora Leigh, ii.

'''wakiki''' (wak′i-ki), ''n.'' A variety of shell-money used in New Caledonia and other islands of the Pacific. Compare ''wampum.''

'''waking''' (wā′king), ''p. a.'' '''1.''' Being awake; not sleeping.
{{smaller block|If you’re ''waking'' call me early.
{{right|''Tennyson'', May Queen, New Year’s Eve.}}}}

readings.c1s3:
